0..77 Comment "//! The pure λ-calculus as data and its single substitution, the base of the"
78..158 Comment "//! λ-calculus syntax model. `theory LC` is the single-substitution calculus of"
159..177 Comment "//! Kaposi and Xie"
178..271 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics],"
272..349 Comment "//! §7: the presentation `first_order` mints from `theory Lambda`, its names"
350..428 Comment "//! written without the generated `$` and its context arguments implicit, as a"
429..508 Comment "//! `theory` block writes them. The syntax model\'s carriers are de Bruijn terms"
509..589 Comment "//! and two substitution data: a substitution shifts, conses a term onto another"
590..667 Comment "//! or lifts one under a binder, and a renaming shifts or lifts. Lifting is a"
668..740 Comment "//! constructor, so the substitution laws reach their inductive steps by"
741..806 Comment "//! conversion; lifting written as a definition reaches them too."
807..810 Comment "//!"
811..887 Comment "//! The argument, file by file: this base; the laws that hold by computation"
888..965 Comment "//! (`sub-q-single`, `sub-q-lift`, `sub-lam`, `sub-app`); the congruences and"
966..1040 Comment "//! the lemmas laws 3 and 4 are proved from (`congruence`, `shift-lookup`,"
1041..1109 Comment "//! `rename-rename`, `lookup-weaken`, `subst-rename`, `subst-subst`,"
1110..1180 Comment "//! `lift-as-definition`, `subst-id`, `subst-as-rename`); laws 3 and 4"
1181..1243 Comment "//! (`sub-weaken-lift`, `sub-weaken-single`); the syntax model"
1244..1310 Comment "//! (`syntax-model`) and the record of `LC`\'s models it packs into"
1311..1332 Comment "//! (`model-record`)."
1333..1336 Comment "//!"
1337..1352 Comment "//! - see: #640"
1353..1369 Comment "//! - see: #2422"
1370..1471 Comment "//! - cites: [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]"
1472..1475 Comment "//!"
1476..1675 Comment "//! [Kaposi-2024-secondorder_generalised_algebraic_theories_signatures_firstorder_semantics]: https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10 \"Kaposi and Xie, Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories\""
1677..1716 Comment "// The naturals, the de Bruijn indices."
